{{Quote|It's their planet. ''We're'' the hostiles.|Han Solo, to Imperial Lieutenant Bolandin|<ref name="Solo" />}}
The '''Mimbanese''' were one of several [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Mimban]]. Experts in guerrilla warfare, the Mimbanese had the unsettling ability to seemingly disappear into the mud and murk of their homeworld.<ref name="The Official Guide" />

==Biology and appearance==
[[File:IasentoFull-BTCG.png|thumb|250px|left|Iasento, leader of the Mimbanese Liberation Army]]
The Mimbanese, also known as the Mimbanites, were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] [[Homeworld|native]] to the [[planet]] [[Mimban]].<ref name="The Official Guide" /> The Mimbanese had lurid, [[Color|red]] skin, lidless blue [[eye]]s, and two row of short horns above their brows.<ref name="Solo" /> The Mimbanese could also be brown<ref name="Bounty Hunters 15" /> or grey skinned.<ref name="AcolyteVG" /> The Mimbanese had enhanced eyesight, adapted to the low light of their homes.<ref name="Alien Archive">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref> The bright red color of the Mimbanese came from their keratin scutes, although they could fade in color.<ref name="AcolyteVG" />

==Society and culture==
The Mimbanese were one of several sentient species that inhabited Mimban.<ref name="The Official Guide" /> The Mimbanese lived underground, and were experts in camouflage. The Mimbanese were both highly aggressive and highly intelligent,<ref name="Alien Archive" /> being capable of creating improvised traps and covering themselves in mud for camouflage.<ref name="The Official Guide" />

==History==
{{Quote|We needed a swamp native to interface with the Mimbanese.|[[Clone Captain]] [[Rex]], to [[Hardcase]]|<ref name="501+1">{{StoryCite|story=501 Plus One|book=Age of Republic Special 1}}</ref>}}
[[File:MimbaneseTrio-SoloASWS.png|thumb|300px|right|A trio of Mimbanese soldiers]]
Though Mimban was ignored by the greater [[galaxy]] for most of its history,<ref name="Alien Archive" /> the Mimbanese eventually made contact with the [[Galactic Republic]] by the time of the [[High Republic Era]].<ref name="Light of the Jedi">''[[The High Republic: Light of the Jedi]]''</ref> During this time, several members of the species would go on to join the [[Nihil]].<ref name="The High Republic: Midnight Horizon">''[[The High Republic: Midnight Horizon]]''</ref>

During the [[Clone Wars]], the Mimbanese allied themselves with the [[Grand Army of the Republic|Grand Army]] of the Galactic Republic. Under the leadership of tribal leader [[Iasento]], the Mimbanese organized a [[Mimbanese Liberation Army|Liberation Army]].<ref name="The Official Guide" /> [[Junior Representative]] [[Jar Jar Binks]] was sent to help the [[501st Legion|501st]] interface with the Mimbanese.<ref name="501+1" /> With aid from the [[Mud Jumpers]] of the Grand Army's [[224th Imperial Armored Division|224th division]], the Mimbanese [[Battle of Mimban|fought]] the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] and were successful in repelling the Separatists from Mimban.<ref name="The Official Guide" />

Following the Republic's [[Proclamation of the New Order|transformation]] into the [[Galactic Empire]], the Mimbanese [[Mimban Campaign|fought]] [[swamp trooper]]s from the Empire's 224th Imperial Armored Division.<ref name="Solo" />

==Mimbanese in the galaxy==
Iasento was a [[Gender|male]] Mimbanese tribal leader who helped to organize and lead the Mimbanese Liberation Army during the Clone Wars.<ref name="The Official Guide /> He would later lead the army against the [[Imperial Army|Empire's forces]] during the [[Imperial Era]].<ref name="Solo" />

[[Waydurk]]<ref name="Card Trader">{{SWCT|set=The Cloud-Riders|cardname=Waydurk}}</ref> was a Mimbanese who joined the [[Cloud-Riders]] after seeing his homeworld become subjugated by the Empire.<ref name="Solo" />

[[Kierah Koovah]] was a Mimbanese who allied with the Galactic Republic during the Battle of Mimban during which she lost an arm. At one point she was equipped with a [[Cybernetics|cybernetic]] replacement for the arm. Following the [[Battle of Endor]], Koovah allied with the [[New Republic]] and became the [[Vanguard Leader|leader]] of [[Vanguard Squadron]], [[pilot]]ing a [[UT-60D U-wing starfighter/support craft|U-wing]].<ref name="Squadrons" />

